cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PLENA, please cite the software and the accompanying article."
type: software
title: "PLENA: Program for Large-scale Evaluation of Network Analysis"
url: "https://github.com/seokminsu99-byte/FMT_plug_PLENA"
repository-code: "https://github.com/seokminsu99-byte/FMT_plug_PLENA"
license: "MIT"
abstract: >-
  PLENA is a C++17 implementation of a one-parameter Gibbs model for
  stochastic structural analysis of drainage networks, outlet-referenced
  width-function calculation, and beta-class estimation using Nash-Sutcliffe
  efficiency.
keywords:
  - urban drainage networks
  - Gibbs model
  - stochastic network analysis
  - width function
  - computational hydrology
authors:
